<headroom-library version="1" id="clean-funk-snap" category="Clean" order="90" instrument="guitar" style="Funk">
  <description>Bright, tightly compressed chank for 16th-note funk and disco: a fast FET limiter feeds a clean blackface twin with treble high and bass low, blended with a crisp direct signal the way session players track it. No reverb, so every muted scratch stays tight. Neck/middle pickups; DI Blend sets the glassy edge.</description>
  <tags><tag>Clean</tag><tag>Funk</tag><tag>Compressed</tag><tag>Direct</tag><tag>Disco</tag></tags>
  <sources>
    <source url="https://www.guitarplayer.com/gear/i-only-play-one-guitar-nile-rodgers-riffs-on-his-famed-hitmaker" title="Guitar Player: Nile Rodgers on the Hitmaker (direct signal blended with the amp)"/>
    <source url="https://gearspace.com/threads/clean-nile-rodgers-disco-tone-through-interface.1142699/" title="Gearspace: Nile Rodgers disco tone through an interface (DI, console, compressor)"/>
    <source url="https://www.musicradar.com/news/cory-wong-the-key-to-it-all-the-starting-point-for-understanding-is-just-to-listen" title="MusicRadar: Cory Wong interview (position 4, always-on compressor, records DI)"/>
    <source url="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jimmy_Nolen" title="Jimmy Nolen (Wikipedia)"/>
  </sources>
</headroom-library>
</headroom-preset>
